impact-intro = The rings are the published diameters. A moose or roe outline is not drawn, because those shapes are not measured yet. The controls choose the target, the range, and the uncertainty bars. They do not zoom the picture.
impact-target-tip = Which ring set to draw. Moose and roe use the published diameters. Custom uses the diameter you type.
impact-range-tip = Range of the point of impact. Changing it moves the mark on the target. The button beside the number is the length unit, not a zoom control.
impact-mv-tip = Muzzle-velocity standard deviation. The vertical bar is the path at plus and minus this speed. The button beside the number is the speed unit.
impact-error-tip = How far the range estimate can be wrong. The short ticks are the path at the range plus and minus this distance. The button beside the number is the length unit.
impact-wind-tip = Extra wind speeds, from 9 o'clock. Each speed draws a circle on the wind line. This is not a zoom control.
impact-zone-tip = Diameter of a custom target. Used only when the target is Custom diameter. The button beside the number is the length unit.
